[Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  the uh  indiana hoosiers 4-0 right now their  head coach is tom allen who joins us on  the program coach congratulations how  surprised are you that you're 4-0 right  now going into the ohio state game  well thanks dan appreciate you having me  you know um  i'm not going to sit here and tell you  i'm surprised because i'm not you know  our team has built into this point for  the last several years uh i'm sure not  everybody agrees  with my assessment but uh in terms of  our locker room and our players  if you talk to them they would give you  a similar response your voice sounds  about  eight games into a season not four games  into a season coach  you got to take care of that voice yeah  i need to but i don't do a very good job  of that i do quite a bit of yelling  you do do the players understand like if  you yell  do the players know they're in trouble  or they're they're just that's how you  you coach them well they'll know the  difference i'm usually pretty loud  in general but it'll change in tone when  it's  not positive but uh i just i like coach  with a lot of energy  so i do a lot of communicating with our  team and try to reinforce  the good and the bad well also no fans  so the players can't say hey i didn't  hear you coach  that's right they can hear everything  now  what did you think when you watch the  ohio state tapes  it's impressive you know the thing that  jumps out to me is just  justin fields i mean he just he never  hardly throws any incompletions i mean  it's  it's amazing how he's so accurate and uh  he's just playing at an extremely high  level you know they're always every year  we play them  um they look similar in terms of they're  just so big and physical  a lot of great athletes scheme is really  really good  very well coached you know so but you  know when you got a player like jessica  that's why i thought last year's team  was different  than the previous teams we played  against uh because of his ability to  throw the football so accurately  so effectively and in his athleticism is  his elite as well so  he's what makes them really really  special i think makes them different  than when dwayne haskins was there  yeah because he can run it and throw it  you know dwayne was just a  passer and the run-through wasn't the  same whereas now  you have the the passing ability uh and  the running ability that i think is  is extremely high level so it puts a ton  of stress on the defense  what is your message do you already know  what you're going to say to your team  before they take the field against ohio  state  i got an idea it kind of builds  throughout the week i kind of you know  take a lot in pray about it ponder a lot  of things  figure out what they need to hear at  that moment obviously if the preparation  matters more  than that final you know charge to our  team but  but at the same time you know we got to  play with the ton of confidence and  and uh we just got to go there let it  rip you know it's a great opportunity  for sure but we're playing the team that  uh  in the end hasn't beaten very frequently  in the past maybe you should watch uh  miracle on ice with her brooks and get  that speech and maybe uh  maybe sprinkled that in your kids might  not be aware of that speech coach so you  could sample from herb brooks and maybe  uh  maybe i'll resonate with your kids yeah  you never know but uh  i don't think our guys think it's gonna  take a miracle we just gotta play our  best football  why not an eight-team playoff this year  if you look at  you know what you guys have been through  college football has been through you're  not sure how many games you're going to  play it's not going to be the summer  now same number with the sec and the acc  and big 12.  isn't it really crying out for an 18  playoff this year yeah i would have to  agree with you on that one i think it  would make a ton of sense  uh there's so many things there's going  to be so many inequities with  everybody's schedule  number of games played and how do you  decide what matters or how do you  what number do you come up with uh when  the kids have no  control over any of that so it'd be a  perfect time to  expand it to that number so it doesn't  look like that's going to happen but it  sure would make a whole lot of sense  what was that feeling like in the locker  room when you beat penn state in  overtime  it was unbelievable you know just uh a  culmination of a lot of things you know  this is a  room full of guys that believed in the  vision that we had for this program even  when many did not believe  and these guys did that's why they came  here coach of staff included and  so it was a special special time it was  uh it was a great great feeling  and one i'll never forget it's one thing  when you're a coach and you see one of  your players out there injured it's  another thing i'm sure when  you look out there and you see that it's  your son thomas a reserve linebacker who  got  injured what's that like as not a coach  but a parent when you're watching what's  going on  yeah it rips your heart out you know  it's just uh it is a little different  you know i have to be honest with you  when it's your son  um and i i didn't know at the time how  serious it was but when i got out there  and our medical guys whispered to me  that it was a dislocated hip i was  i couldn't believe it i knew that was  serious injury and so  my heart just sank because i knew this  season was over and obviously even his  whole future was in jeopardy so  uh but you know he's a tough tough kid  and and you got to be able to separate  the two but man i love him my whole  heart and  and he's a special young man we've been  through a lot together so but he had  surgery yesterday  and he's on his road back to recovery  yeah it's one thing for you  you gotta you gotta coach your game how  did mom feel about that uh  watching that's really hard well you  know it's all the travel and everything  so she wasn't even at the game and so  i had our dfo caller immediately uh  because obviously she saw what happened  when watching the game but didn't know  the details and just tried to get her to  to be able to  to stay informed and so that made it  really really difficult on her for sure  so but uh  it's part of being in this profession  and part of being what we do we've kind  of learned to  gotta have thick skin you gotta be tough  how many jobs have you had  uh this is my 11th school that i've been  at that includes high school and college  so  number 11. yeah and you were at  newcastle high school right  that's correct that's where i went to  school played for my dad couple years  after steve alford  yes he's five years older than me i was  a seventh grader when he was a senior  and he would pack so you watched him uh  in that gym what's that gym c  ten thousand ten thousand unbelievable  high school arena how about that ten  thousand  pounds only got twenty thousand what was  it like to watch steve alford in high  school  oh unbelievable yeah every game was sold  out um  i'd sit there and we had keep track of  this they didn't have a three-pointer  back then so i keep track of all of his  points  all the shots all of his free throws he  never missed any free throws  unbelievable  but his dad was a head coach for  basketball obviously and so  uh yeah pretty special time he was so  fun to watch and uh i've always looked  up to him  i wonder what would he have averaged  with a three-point shot back then in  high school  we averaged 37 without it so you had to  think it's got to be  mid-upper 40s which is unbelievable yeah  well who's the biggest name out of  newcastle high school  steve alfred oh okay well if you beat  ohio state  yeah well hey you know  [Laughter]  uh congrats i i'm old enough to remember  when indiana  was competitive back in the 80s i think  the running back  was mike harkrader and i think he ran  for a thousand yards  coach corso was there i go back a long  way  now i grew up an ohio state fan but uh  i i remember when indiana used to be  okay but uh you've brought him back  i mean this is more than bringing him  back this is something indiana football  hadn't seen  in uh a long long long time so  congratulations on that and uh  and good luck against ohio state thank  you dan i sure appreciate it have an  awesome day helio that's tom allen

